    "visibleText": "Breast cancer classification in digital pathology using Python and Deep Learning - PyCon HK Skip to content Menu PyCon HK Conference Highlights Schedule 2024 2023 2022 2021 2020 Fall 2020 Spring 2018 2017 2016 2015 Sponsors 2024 2023 2022 2021 2020 Fall 2018 2017 2016 2015 Communities 2024 2023 2022 Booths 2024 2023 Organizers 2024 2023 2022 Volunteers 2024 2023 2022 2021 2020 Fall 2018 2017 2016 2015 PyCon HK Breast cancer classification in digital pathology using Python and Deep Learning Posted on October 23, 2018 November 7, 2020 Breast cancer is one of the leading cancer-related death causes worldwide, specially for women. In this talk, we will talk about how Deep Learning & Python could help pathologists to classify breast cancer microscopic images. The speaker will share his approach that won the “ ICIAR 2018 Grand Challenge on Breast Cancer Histology images ”, which was implemented in Python. Refer to the papers for more details: https://arxiv.org/abs/1808.04277 https://link.springer.com/chapter/10.1007/978-3-319-93000-8_106 Buzzwords: Deep Learning, Digital Pathology, Breast Cancer, Whole-Slide Images, AI Level: Advanced: Target audiences with advanced experience in python programming Requirements to Audiences: Nil Language: English Speaker: Scotty Kwok (Hong Kong) Speaker Bio: Scotty have been working in IT for 17+ years and is a seasoned developer in Java and Python. He is experienced in using various AI/Deep Learning frameworks (e.g. Keras, PyTorch, etc.) and neural networks (e.g. VGG, Inception, Resnet, etc). Scotty has a passion in solving medical problems and recently he won a global grand challenge in Breast Cancer image classification by using deep learning. Currently, he is on a journey to run a mixed- reality startup, SEBit , with his 3 other partners. GitHub: https://github.com/scottykwok LinkedIn: https://www.linkedin.com/in/scottykwok/ Twitter: https://twitter.com/scottykwok Website/Blog: http://sebit.world Instagram LinkedIn Facebook Twitter YouTube Search for: Archives Archives Select Month November 2024 October 2024 September 2024 July 2024 April 2024 December 2023 October 2023 September 2023 July 2023 April 2023 November 2022 October 2022 August 2022 October 2021 September 2021 May 2021 November 2020 October 2020 September 2020 May 2020 April 2020 November 2018 October 2018 September 2018 August 2018 November 2017 October 2016 November 2015 History 2024 2023 2022 2021 2020-fall 2020-spring 2018 2017 2016 2015 ©2026 PyCon HK | Powered by SuperbThemes! ← Ticket – PyCon HK 2018 ← Announcing 1st round of sessions in 2018"
