    "visibleText": "NoSQL Development for MySQL Document Store using Python - PyCon HK Skip to content Menu PyCon HK Conference Highlights Schedule 2024 2023 2022 2021 2020 Fall 2020 Spring 2018 2017 2016 2015 Sponsors 2024 2023 2022 2021 2020 Fall 2018 2017 2016 2015 Communities 2024 2023 2022 Booths 2024 2023 Organizers 2024 2023 2022 Volunteers 2024 2023 2022 2021 2020 Fall 2018 2017 2016 2015 PyCon HK NoSQL Development for MySQL Document Store using Python Posted on October 28, 2018 September 18, 2024 MySQL 8.0 introduced the MySQL Document Store, allowing developers to work with SQL relational tables and schema-less JSON collections through the use of the X DevAPI. Join us to better understand how MySQL Connector/Python implements and makes use of the X DevAPI along with a quick demo showcasing its most relevant features. Additionally, concepts such as the X Protocol, NoSQL and the aforementioned X DevAPI are reviewed to get better understanding on the MySQL Document Store Level : Intermediate: Target audiences with intermediate experience in python programming Requirements to Audiences : Nil Language : English Speaker: Ivan Ma (Hong Kong) Speaker Bio : Ivan Ma is the MySQL User Group Lead in Hong Kong. He has over 20+ years of experience in enterprise system infrastructure and software technologies. He has certification on MySQL DBA 5.6, MySQL Developer 5.1 and MySQL Cluster 5.1 DBA. He Joined MySQL, is currently MySQL Principal Sales Consultant, Asia Pacific with Oracle, responsible for pre-sales consulting, technical education, and product promotions. Prior to joining MySQL team, he joined Oracle in System Team from Sun Mircosystems acquisition. Prior to Sun Microsystems, he was Principal Solution Architect with Sybase APAC covering APAC regions. Website/Blog : mysqlhk.blogspot.com Instagram LinkedIn Facebook Twitter YouTube Search for: Archives Archives Select Month November 2024 October 2024 September 2024 July 2024 April 2024 December 2023 October 2023 September 2023 July 2023 April 2023 November 2022 October 2022 August 2022 October 2021 September 2021 May 2021 November 2020 October 2020 September 2020 May 2020 April 2020 November 2018 October 2018 September 2018 August 2018 November 2017 October 2016 November 2015 History 2024 2023 2022 2021 2020-fall 2020-spring 2018 2017 2016 2015 ©2026 PyCon HK | Powered by SuperbThemes! ← Ready, Get Set, Go! Development Sprints in Python community ← Deploying Django App On AWS Lambda – Serverless Architecture"
